---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import '../styles/system.css';

const title = 'Trust Center — Pilot Protocol';
const description = 'Pilot Protocol security, architecture, deployment controls, metric definitions, and technical references in one place.';
const canonicalUrl = 'https://pilotprotocol.network/trust';
---
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <BaseHead title={title} description={description} canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl} />
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify({
    '@context': 'https://schema.org',
    '@type': 'WebPage',
    name: title,
    description,
    url: canonicalUrl,
    about: {
      '@type': 'SoftwareApplication',
      name: 'Pilot Protocol',
      applicationCategory: 'NetworkingApplication',
      license: 'https://www.gnu.org/licenses/agpl-3.0.html',
    },
  })}></script>
</head>
<body>

<Nav active="trust" />

<main>
  <section class="trust-hero">
    <div class="gridbg" aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="eyebrow">Trust Center</div>
      <h1>Security and control,<br/> <em>built into the <span class="keep-word">network.</span></em></h1>
      <p class="trust-lede">Explore how Pilot handles identity, encrypted transport, trust, coordination, policy, and audit across core and managed deployments.</p>
      <div class="trust-actions">
        <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/security">Security documentation <span class="arr">→</span></a>
        <a class="btn" href="/governance">Governance model</a>
        <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/pilot-protocol/pilotprotocol" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Inspect the source</a>
        <a class="btn" href="/security/disclosure">Report a vulnerability</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="trust-summary" aria-label="Pilot Protocol status summary">
    <div class="wrap summary-grid">
      <div class="summary-item">
        <span class="summary-label">Source</span>
        <strong>AGPL-3.0</strong>
        <span>Daemon and protocol implementation are public.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="summary-item">
        <span class="summary-label">Private-node access</span>
        <strong>Trust or network policy</strong>
        <span>Application traffic requires an applicable grant.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="summary-item">
        <span class="summary-label">Specification</span>
        <strong>Public wire format</strong>
        <span>Implementation-aligned technical reference.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="summary-item">
        <span class="summary-label">Enterprise</span>
        <strong>Early access</strong>
        <span>Managed controls are available for evaluation.</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="architecture">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-copy">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Architecture</div>
          <h2>Peer connectivity.<br/> <em>Lightweight coordination.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <p>Pilot separates encrypted agent traffic from the services used for identity registration, discovery, NAT traversal, and relay fallback.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture-map" aria-label="Pilot Protocol control-plane and data-plane architecture">
        <div class="map-node map-agent">
          <span class="map-kicker">Endpoint</span>
          <strong>Agent A</strong>
          <span>Ed25519 identity</span>
        </div>
        <div class="map-center">
          <div class="map-lane control-lane">
            <span class="lane-name">Coordination plane</span>
            <strong>Registry + beacon</strong>
            <span>Discovery, public keys, endpoint exchange, NAT assistance</span>
            <small>Pilot-operated by default · endpoints are configurable</small>
          </div>
          <div class="map-lane data-lane">
            <span class="lane-name">Payload plane</span>
            <strong>Encrypted peer tunnel</strong>
            <span>X25519 key exchange · AES-256-GCM tunnel</span>
            <small>Direct when possible · encrypted relay fallback when needed</small>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="map-node map-agent">
          <span class="map-kicker">Endpoint</span>
          <strong>Agent B</strong>
          <span>Ed25519 identity</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="architecture-notes">
        <div><b>What coordination can see</b><span>Registration metadata, public keys, advertised endpoints, timing, and network membership needed to operate the service.</span></div>
        <div><b>What relay fallback carries</b><span>Encrypted payload packets. The relay adds a hop and can observe traffic metadata, but it does not receive tunnel keys.</span></div>
        <div><b>What you can change</b><span>Registry and beacon endpoints are configuration values. Dedicated and on-premises deployments are enterprise early access.</span></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" id="governance">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-copy">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Governance boundary</div>
          <h2>Network controls for<br/> <em>real-world workflows.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <p>Pilot authenticates peers and constrains network access. Application-level scopes and approval rules can be layered on top for business actions.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="boundary-table" aria-label="Pilot and application responsibility boundary">
        <div class="boundary-column pilot-column">
          <div class="column-head"><span>Pilot enforces</span><b>Network authority</b></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Persistent agent identity and signed handshakes</li>
            <li>Private-node stream and datagram admission</li>
            <li>Peer trust, network membership, rejection, and revocation</li>
            <li>Network membership and port policies</li>
            <li>Role-based administration and key lifecycle</li>
            <li>Structured network and security audit events</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="boundary-column app-column">
          <div class="column-head"><span>Your system enforces</span><b>Business authority</b></div>
          <ul>
            <li>Which tasks an agent is allowed to perform</li>
            <li>Purchase limits and counterparty approval</li>
            <li>Human review for consequential actions</li>
            <li>Data classification and retention rules</li>
            <li>Prompt, model, and tool-level safety controls</li>
            <li>Legal, regulatory, and contractual compliance</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="governance-callout">
        <span class="callout-mark">!</span>
        <p><b>Layer controls around consequential actions.</b> Cross-company workflows can combine Pilot network policy with application-level scopes, spend or order caps, and approval gates. <a href="/governance">Review the full governance model →</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="controls">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-copy">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Control surface</div>
          <h2>Controls a security team<br/> <em>can evaluate.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <p>Core protocol controls ship in the open-source daemon. Private and enterprise operations are early access and should be evaluated against your production requirements.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="control-grid">
        <a href="/docs/trust" class="control-card"><span>Core · available</span><h3>Trust & revocation</h3><p>Private nodes admit application traffic through peer trust or shared-network membership, with reject and revoke controls.</p></a>
        <a href="/docs/security" class="control-card"><span>Core · available</span><h3>Encrypted transport</h3><p>Ed25519 identity, X25519 key agreement, and AES-256-GCM authenticated tunnels.</p></a>
        <a href="/docs/enterprise-rbac" class="control-card"><span>Enterprise · early access</span><h3>RBAC & key lifecycle</h3><p>Owner, admin, and member roles; delegated administration; rotation, expiry, and forced renewal.</p></a>
        <a href="/docs/enterprise-identity" class="control-card"><span>Enterprise · early access</span><h3>Identity integration</h3><p>Native OIDC/JWT validation, provider webhooks, directory sync, role mapping, and bridge paths for other identity systems.</p></a>
        <a href="/docs/enterprise-policies" class="control-card"><span>Enterprise · early access</span><h3>Network policy</h3><p>Membership limits, port allowlists, join rules, policy expressions, and fail-closed policy retention.</p></a>
        <a href="/docs/enterprise-audit" class="control-card"><span>Enterprise · early access</span><h3>Audit export</h3><p>Structured events with export to Splunk HEC, CEF/Syslog, JSON endpoints, and webhooks.</p></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" id="claims">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-copy">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Product status</div>
          <h2>Capabilities and<br/> <em>availability.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <p>A concise view of shipped functionality, early-access controls, and the responsibilities that remain at the application layer.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="claims-table">
        <div class="claim-row claim-head"><span>Topic</span><span>Status</span><span>Precise statement</span></div>
        <div class="claim-row"><b>Protocol implementation</b><span class="status shipped">Available</span><p>Source is published under AGPL-3.0 and can be inspected, modified, and redistributed under that license.</p></div>
        <div class="claim-row"><b>Wire specification</b><span class="status shipped">Published</span><p>The protocol message types, addressing, transport, encryption, and trust model are available for technical review alongside the implementation.</p></div>
        <div class="claim-row"><b>Pre-trust hardening</b><span class="status shipped">Configurable</span><p>Optional strict controls extend trust checks to key exchange, private directory operations, and NAT-punch authorization. They are enabled per deployment after compatibility review.</p></div>
        <div class="claim-row"><b>Private / enterprise networks</b><span class="status early">Early access</span><p>Managed and dedicated deployments, identity integrations, policies, and audit exports are available for evaluation; availability and SLAs are not represented as generally available.</p></div>
        <div class="claim-row"><b>Security certification</b><span class="status none">Current status</span><p>Independent certification is not currently listed. Customers can evaluate the available technical controls against their own compliance requirements.</p></div>
        <div class="claim-row"><b>Business-process governance</b><span class="status none">Application layer</span><p>Pilot governs agent connectivity; application authorization, approval flows, and legal authority are configured by the deploying organization.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" id="apps">
    <div class="wrap split-detail">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">App Store</div>
        <h2>Curated packages.<br/> <em>Layered control.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="detail-copy">
        <p>Listed apps are reviewed and verified before discovery, while network trust and application policy continue to shape access at runtime.</p>
        <ul>
          <li>App review answers whether a listing meets catalogue requirements.</li>
          <li>Network trust answers whether two endpoints may communicate.</li>
          <li>Application policy answers what methods, data, spend, and side effects are allowed.</li>
        </ul>
        <a href="/docs/app-store">Read the App Store model →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section-alt" id="metrics">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="section-copy">
        <div>
          <div class="eyebrow">Metric definitions</div>
          <h2>How network activity<br/> <em>is measured.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <p>Homepage figures come from the public network telemetry endpoint. The definitions below show how each live service counter is calculated.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="metric-grid">
        <div class="metric-card"><code>total_nodes</code><h3>Registered agent addresses</h3><p>Cumulative addresses issued by the public registry, rather than a unique organization or customer count.</p></div>
        <div class="metric-card"><code>active_nodes</code><h3>Agents online now</h3><p>Agents currently represented as active by the registry heartbeat state. This counter can change rapidly.</p></div>
        <div class="metric-card"><code>requests_per_sec × 3,600</code><h3>Protocol requests per hour</h3><p>A rate derived from current registry telemetry. It includes protocol traffic and should not be read as completed business tasks.</p></div>
      </div>
      <p class="metric-source">Source: <a href="https://polo.pilotprotocol.network/api/public-stats" target="_blank" rel="noopener">public network telemetry JSON</a>. Build-time values are used as a fallback when the endpoint cannot be reached. These operational counters have not undergone independent audit.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section trust-close">
    <div class="wrap close-grid">
      <div>
        <div class="eyebrow">Evaluate Pilot</div>
        <h2>Start with the<br/> <em>technical model.</em></h2>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p>Review the implementation, test inside an isolated network, define the application authority your agents will retain, and bring the evidence to your security team.</p>
        <div class="trust-actions">
          <a class="btn primary" href="/docs/security">Review security <span class="arr">→</span></a>
          <a class="btn" href="/enterprise-readiness-report.pdf">Readiness report (PDF)</a>
          <a class="btn" href="/contact?topic=security-review">Contact the team</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</main>

<Footer />

<style>
  .trust-hero { position: relative; overflow: hidden; padding: 110px 0 96px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .trust-hero .wrap { position: relative; z-index: 1; }
  .trust-hero h1 { max-width: 1100px; margin: 18px 0 28px; font-size: clamp(58px, 8vw, 128px); line-height: .9; letter-spacing: -.05em; }
  .trust-hero h1 em, h2 em { font-family: var(--serif); font-weight: 400; }
  .keep-word { white-space: nowrap; }
  .trust-lede { max-width: 760px; color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: clamp(19px, 2vw, 25px); line-height: 1.5; }
  .trust-actions { display: flex; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; margin-top: 34px; }
  .trust-summary { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg-deep); }
  .summary-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); }
  .summary-item { display: flex; flex-direction: column; min-height: 190px; padding: 28px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .summary-item:last-child { border-right: 0; }
  .summary-label, .map-kicker, .lane-name, .control-card > span { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent-text); }
  .summary-item strong { margin: auto 0 8px; font-size: 22px; }
  .summary-item > span:last-child { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .section-alt { background: var(--bg-deep); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .section-copy { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1.1fr .9fr; gap: 80px; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 52px; }
  .section-copy h2, .split-detail h2, .close-grid h2 { margin-top: 14px; font-size: clamp(44px, 5.8vw, 84px); line-height: .97; letter-spacing: -.045em; }
  .section-copy > p { max-width: 48ch; color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: clamp(18px, 1.8vw, 22px); line-height: 1.55; }
  .architecture-map { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 220px 1fr 220px; gap: 18px; align-items: stretch; }
  .map-node, .map-lane { border: 1px solid var(--line-2); background: var(--bg); }
  .map-node { display: flex; flex-direction: column; justify-content: center; min-height: 300px; padding: 26px; text-align: center; }
  .map-node strong { margin: 18px 0 8px; font-size: 28px; }
  .map-node > span:last-child { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 13px; }
  .map-center { display: grid; grid-template-rows: 1fr 1fr; gap: 18px; }
  .map-lane { position: relative; display: grid; grid-template-columns: 160px 1fr; gap: 8px 24px; padding: 25px 30px; }
  .map-lane::before, .map-lane::after { content: ''; position: absolute; top: 50%; width: 19px; height: 1px; background: var(--accent); }
  .map-lane::before { left: -19px; }
  .map-lane::after { right: -19px; }
  .map-lane strong { font-size: 20px; }
  .map-lane > span:not(.lane-name) { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 14px; }
  .map-lane small { grid-column: 2; color: var(--ink-dim); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .data-lane { border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 55%, var(--line)); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 6%, var(--bg)); }
  .architecture-notes { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); margin-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .architecture-notes > div { padding: 24px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .architecture-notes b { display: block; margin-bottom: 10px; font-size: 15px; }
  .architecture-notes span { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .boundary-table { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; border: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
  .boundary-column { padding: 34px; }
  .boundary-column + .boundary-column { border-left: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
  .column-head { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; padding-bottom: 28px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .column-head span { color: var(--ink-dim); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .column-head b { font-size: 28px; }
  .boundary-column ul { margin: 24px 0 0; list-style: none; }
  .boundary-column li { position: relative; padding: 10px 0 10px 26px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--ink-dim); }
  .boundary-column li::before { content: '✓'; position: absolute; left: 0; color: var(--accent); }
  .app-column li::before { content: '→'; }
  .governance-callout { display: flex; gap: 20px; align-items: center; margin-top: 18px; padding: 24px 28px; border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 45%, var(--line)); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 6%, var(--bg)); }
  .callout-mark { display: grid; place-items: center; flex: none; width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; background: var(--accent); color: var(--accent-ink); font-family: var(--mono); font-weight: 800; }
  .governance-callout p { color: var(--ink-dim); }
  .governance-callout b { color: var(--ink); }
  .control-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-left: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .control-card { min-height: 260px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; padding: 28px; border-right: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); background: var(--bg); color: var(--ink); }
  .control-card:hover { color: var(--ink); background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 5%, var(--bg)); }
  .control-card h3 { margin: auto 0 12px; font-size: 24px; }
  .control-card p { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .claims-table { border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
  .claim-row { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 230px 150px 1fr; gap: 26px; align-items: start; padding: 22px 18px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .claim-row p { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .claim-head { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 10px; letter-spacing: .12em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--ink-dim); }
  .status { justify-self: start; padding: 4px 9px; border: 1px solid var(--line-2); font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 9px; letter-spacing: .08em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .status.shipped { color: var(--accent-text); border-color: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent) 45%, var(--line)); }
  .status.draft, .status.early { color: #f2b45a; border-color: color-mix(in srgb, #f2b45a 45%, var(--line)); }
  :global([data-theme="light"]) .status.draft,
  :global([data-theme="light"]) .status.early { color: #7a4b00; border-color: #9b650e; }
  .status.none { color: var(--ink-dim); }
  .split-detail, .close-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 80px; }
  .detail-copy { padding-top: 30px; }
  .detail-copy p, .close-grid p { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; }
  .detail-copy ul { margin: 26px 0; list-style: none; }
  .detail-copy li { padding: 12px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); color: var(--ink-dim); }
  .detail-copy a { color: var(--accent-text); }
  .metric-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 18px; }
  .metric-card { padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line-2); background: var(--bg); }
  .metric-card code { color: var(--accent-text); }
  .metric-card h3 { margin: 54px 0 12px; font-size: 23px; }
  .metric-card p { color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .metric-source { margin-top: 20px; color: var(--ink-dim); font-size: 13px; }
  .metric-source a { color: var(--accent-text); }
  .trust-close { padding-top: 110px; padding-bottom: 110px; }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .summary-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; }
    .summary-item:nth-child(2) { border-right: 0; }
    .summary-item:nth-child(-n+2) { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .section-copy, .split-detail, .close-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 26px; }
    .architecture-map { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .map-node { min-height: 160px; }
    .map-lane::before, .map-lane::after { display: none; }
    .architecture-notes, .control-grid, .metric-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .boundary-table { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .boundary-column + .boundary-column { border-left: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line-2); }
  }
  @media (max-width: 680px) {
    .trust-hero { padding: 72px 0 62px; }
    .trust-hero h1 { font-size: clamp(48px, 14vw, 72px); }
    .summary-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .summary-item { min-height: 150px; border-right: 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
    .summary-item:last-child { border-bottom: 0; }
    .map-lane { grid-template-columns: 1fr; padding: 22px; }
    .map-lane small { grid-column: 1; }
    .claim-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 10px; padding: 22px 0; }
    .claim-head { display: none; }
    .boundary-column { padding: 24px; }
    .governance-callout { align-items: flex-start; }
  }
</style>

</body>
</html>
